kindspec/.github is licensed per directory. This is deliberate, not an oversight.

  scripts/                  MIT
  everything else           CC-BY-4.0

"Everything else" is the documents: AGENTS.md, STATE.md, README.md, profile/
(including the org mark in profile/assets/), the issue forms in
.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/, and configuration such as .gitignore. This file is part
of it. The licence texts in LICENSES/ are not: each is published under its own
terms by its steward.

Full texts are in LICENSES/. Source files carry SPDX headers.

WHY THE SPLIT

Prose under CC-BY-4.0, so the contract can be copied and adapted with
attribution; code under MIT. The contract is meant to be reused — a rule other
projects can lift is worth more than one they have to rewrite. Each kindspec
repository states its own split in its own LICENSE; this one describes this
repository only.
